      "en": "Georges Friedmann comments that so long as this world is still frequented by men, by comrades, there is a chance of conquering it, of moulding it to the ends of culture and dignity. Nothing could be more true, I think, but we must still ask ourselves on what terms this comradeship can remain genuine. It stares us in the face that it is in grave danger of being impaired by the intrusion of politics, or if you like of propaganda."
