      "en": "The Characteristics of Technical Progress It is evident that the mastery of the forces of nature by means of increasingly elaborate technical processes is a liberation which should be welcomed as such; but it is no less true that, for reasons which must be examined, this liberation is in danger of being itself turned into a slavery. It is in this contradiction that the drama of industrial civilisation lies. Going back to the ambiguity I mentioned at the beginning, I would say that, again for the same reasons, this particular civilisation is in danger of developing against certain universal values which would seem to be a part of civilisation in general."
